WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:05.492
Edward and Miles were put into a cell together.

2
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:11.924
Edward stood at the bars, calling for the guard, while Miles sat sadly in a corner.

3
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:15.583
"I demand to be released!" Edward shouted.

4
00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:21.086
"You have no right to imprison me! I'm the king!"

5
00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:25.970
"And I'm the emperor!" a prisoner in another cell shouted.

6
00:00:25.971 --> 00:00:35.216
There were roars of laughter from other prisoners.

7
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:40.498
Edward went over to sit on the floor beside Miles. "How are you feeling?"

8
00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:47.580
Miles sighed. "I thought everyone at Hendon Hall would be happy to see me.

9
00:00:47.581 --> 00:00:53.106
Instead no one seemed to recognize me, and I wound up here.

10
00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:56.568
I don't know whether to laugh or cry."

11
00:00:56.569 --> 00:00:59.321
Edward put an arm around his friend.

12
00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:06.326
"You always get us out of trouble, Sir Miles. Maybe we can escape?"

13
00:01:06.327 --> 00:01:09.615
But Miles was too discouraged to try.

14
00:01:09.616 --> 00:01:15.638
He spent the rest of the day thinking about Edith.

15
00:01:15.639 --> 00:01:21.037
"I'm sure Edith recognized me," he said to Edward as they ate dinner.

16
00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:25.634
"But something—or someone—made her lie."

17
00:01:25.635 --> 00:01:28.515
"There's only one thing I'm sure of."

18
00:01:28.516 --> 00:01:32.793
Edward made a face as he swallowed a spoonful of brown glop.

19
00:01:32.794 --> 00:01:40.918
"This is the worst food I've ever tasted."

20
00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:46.863
The next day an old man carrying a basket came to visit all the prisoners.

21
00:01:46.864 --> 00:01:50.531
He handed fresh bread into each cell.

22
00:01:50.532 --> 00:01:55.890
"Blake Andrews! My former servant!" Miles cried happily.

23
00:01:55.891 --> 00:01:58.378
"You must recognize me!"

24
00:01:58.379 --> 00:02:03.874
"Shh!" Blake looked around to be sure no one was listening.

25
00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:07.042
"Thank goodness you've returned.

26
00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:13.567
I never believed you were dead, so when I heard you were here, I had to see for myself."

27
00:02:13.568 --> 00:02:17.070
Blake patted his basket of bread.

28
00:02:17.071 --> 00:02:21.691
"That's why I'm paying a charitable visit to the prisoners."

29
00:02:21.692 --> 00:02:27.209
"Clever man!" Miles reached through the bars for some bread.

30
00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.797
"Now tell me what's been going on."

31
00:02:30.798 --> 00:02:37.030
Blake explained that soon after Miles' brother Arthur died, Sir Richard became ill.

32
00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:43.132
"When your father received the letter about your death, he lost his will to live.

33
00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:48.776
He urged Hugh and Edith to marry before he passed away."

34
00:02:48.777 --> 00:02:54.943
"And she obviously agreed to that." Miles shook his head sadly.

35
00:02:54.944 --> 00:03:01.098
"No, she didn't!" Blake flashed Miles a triumphant smile.

36
00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:09.350
"She always believed that you'd return, so she resisted your father and Hugh's attempts to set a wedding date."

37
00:03:09.351 --> 00:03:16.050
Now it was Miles' turn to smile brightly. "That's my Edith!"

38
00:03:16.051 --> 00:03:24.598
Edward broke off a piece of bread. "So, how did she end up marrying Hugh?"

39
00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:30.981
"She finally gave in when Sir Richard was on his deathbed," Blake said.

40
00:03:30.982 --> 00:03:34.657
"And she's been unhappy ever since."

41
00:03:34.658 --> 00:03:39.502
"Oh, my darling Edith!" Miles whispered.

42
00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:43.251
Blake leaned close to the bars and spoke softly.

43
00:03:43.252 --> 00:03:49.785
"It's rumored that after the wedding, she found a rough draft of that letter in Hugh's desk.

44
00:03:49.786 --> 00:03:58.429
She accused Hugh of rushing the wedding—and causing Sir Richard's death—by writing the letter himself."

45
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:02.156
"I can believe that," Edward said.

46
00:04:02.157 --> 00:04:12.070
"As soon as Sir Richard died, Hugh began treating everyone cruelly— the servants, the villagers, anyone who depended upon him."

47
00:04:12.071 --> 00:04:17.204
Blake hesitated for a moment. "Even Edith."

48
00:04:17.205 --> 00:04:22.811
This was too much for Miles, who grabbed the cell bars and tried to shake them.

49
00:04:22.812 --> 00:04:28.192
"I'll rescue Edith, if it's the last thing I do!"

50
00:04:28.193 --> 00:04:32.961
The next day Blake returned with more bread and more news.

51
00:04:32.962 --> 00:04:37.938
"The king will be crowned later this week," Blake said.

52
00:04:37.939 --> 00:04:44.723
Edward pulled on Miles' sleeve. "We have to go back to the city right now!"

53
00:04:44.724 --> 00:04:51.413
"I've heard that the king has an illness that affects his mind," Blake went on.

54
00:04:51.414 --> 00:04:54.092
Edward glared at the old man.

55
00:04:54.093 --> 00:05:02.200
"The king is in perfectly good health! I command you to stop this gossip right now!"

56
00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:07.407
Blake gestured toward Edward. "What's the boy talking about?"

57
00:05:07.408 --> 00:05:12.265
Miles shook his head. "It's not important."

58
00:05:12.266 --> 00:05:17.589
"Well, at least the king is kind and merciful," Blake said.

59
00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:24.498
"He spared the Duke of Norfolk's life, and now he's abolishing laws that oppress the poor."

60
00:05:24.499 --> 00:05:28.502
"Who is this king?" Edward thought.

61
00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:36.252
"Even if Tom tried to pass himself off as me, he couldn't keep up that act for long."

62
00:05:36.253 --> 00:05:41.133
Blake returned to the subject of the coronation and said Hugh would be attending.

63
00:05:41.134 --> 00:05:47.240
"He hopes the king will make him an earl because Hugh is friends with Lord Hertford."

64
00:05:47.241 --> 00:05:54.695
Edward started at the name of his adviser. "We'll see about that!" he said.

65
00:05:54.696 --> 00:05:59.351
After Blake left, two more prisoners were put into the cell.

66
00:05:59.352 --> 00:06:05.971
When Edward learned they were wrongly accused of crimes and sentenced to death, he was outraged.

67
00:06:05.972 --> 00:06:10.974
"Miles, we have to get to the coronation," he whispered excitedly.

68
00:06:10.975 --> 00:06:17.125
"After I'm crowned, I can pardon these men and save their lives!"

69
00:06:17.126 --> 00:06:19.898
Miles patted Edward's head.

70
00:06:19.899 --> 00:06:27.438
"First Blake's stories," he thought, "and now these fellows' tales of woe.

71
00:06:27.439 --> 00:06:35.789
I'm afraid everyone's stories have made Edward's illness worse!"

